" /></entry><entry><title>How climate change worsened Nepal's deadly mountain collapse</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f3f21991b0fe6af8e9b9d6f034eb2c1dec08a3607ec5c5749269f4a5c124f489</id><updated>2026-09-17T05:02:21Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T23:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-climate-change-worsened-nepal-s-deadly-mountain-collapse/a-79293578--691d9083ccec.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-climate-change-worsened-nepal-s-deadly-mountain-collapse/a-79293578?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A glacier and rock collapse in Nepal killed nearly 1,400 people and left thousands missing. Scientists say decades of warming helped set the disaster in motion.</summary><category term="Climate" /></entry><entry><title>US Congress passes Russia sanctions bill</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d3aae54bb1a942a1d896161982ece34ab8b55fe322957c7dd044563204a8182c</id><updated>2026-09-17T05:02:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T23:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-congress-passes-russia-sanctions-bill/a-79299088--c37fcf134869.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-congress-passes-russia-sanctions-bill/a-79299088?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The sanctions package is considered the most substantial US legislative effort against Moscow since Trump returned to the White House. Measures in the bill could lead to secondary sanctions on India, China and Iran.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Sweden's center-left bloc set to win election, STV reports</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f7c694957af7da86365e44a5eb86df6cbac70eeb479ed9d8a7f5c20d7f7418ae</id><updated>2026-09-17T05:02:28Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T22:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/sweden-s-center-left-bloc-set-to-win-election-stv-reports/a-79299076--d8d22e208de7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/sweden-s-center-left-bloc-set-to-win-election-stv-reports/a-79299076?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The center-left opposition won the Swedish elections by a very slim margin, the public broadcaster reported after 99% of the votes were counted. Thorny negotiations await the bloc even if the result is confirmed.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US Fed raises key rate for first time in 3 years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:08fad53053e436fa6310ac23279aa343d56443f2c64b2ab974e43894d930c4ca</id><updated>2026-09-17T05:01:18Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T18:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-fed-raises-key-rate-for-first-time-in-3-years/a-79297295--4269b0ad3015.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-fed-raises-key-rate-for-first-time-in-3-years/a-79297295?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In an attempt to address the persistently high inflation in the world's largest economy, the US Federal Reserve increased interest rates by 25 basis points. The president, on the other hand, said they should be cut.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: Oktoberfest beer prices rise, outpacing inflation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2b8dceb863ecc5bfc49fd52dfeae14b4009e5b77cb3890cf27eea059a168bc61</id><updated>2026-09-17T05:01:18Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T18:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-oktoberfest-beer-prices-rise-outpacing-inflation/a-79296932--12fa98bb1113.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-oktoberfest-beer-prices-rise-outpacing-inflation/a-79296932?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Oktoberfest's traditional beer mug, the Mass, will cost an average of €15.61 ($18.50) at this year's festival in Munich.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>UK: Village votes to 'secede' in asylum center plan protest</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b8c7f05e71746c7b71482a4d696eb789b6b336bd8b1fc790042b7db46721365a</id><updated>2026-09-17T05:01:18Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T17:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-village-votes-to-secede-in-asylum-center-plan-protest/a-79295826--f45e2135fb80.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-village-votes-to-secede-in-asylum-center-plan-protest/a-79295826?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Residents of Piddington, a tiny, remote village in Oxfordshire in England, have staged a "referendum" on leaving the UK. They are objecting to plans to open an asylum reception center at a disused military base nearby.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Can Canada and the EU build a deeper partnership?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:702d3ee70b3bf3a9d66d4c9f62d3546b38e64de1d01cadaba237d6115c3b5238</id><updated>2026-09-17T05:01:18Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T16:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-canada-and-the-eu-build-a-deeper-partnership/a-79295388--5b1c7df95a13.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-canada-and-the-eu-build-a-deeper-partnership/a-79295388?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Canadian Prime Minister Carney is known for standing up to US President Donald Trump. Now he wants to forge a "unique alliance" with Europe. But what could such a partnership look like?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Chancellor Merz seeks CDU support as AfD encroaches</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:43e7b2d4c47856c250923d6de3c6f21b07ce93c6f07a556d0952dd2ef218a214</id><updated>2026-09-17T05:01:18Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T16:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/chancellor-merz-seeks-cdu-support-as-afd-encroaches/a-79290192--ce473c897283.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/chancellor-merz-seeks-cdu-support-as-afd-encroaches/a-79290192?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Following the CDU's crushing defeat in the Saxony-Anhalt state election, many are expressing doubts about the party's leader, Chancellor Friedrich Merz. But the CDU doesn't appear to have a viable alternative.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Shock in Kosovo as Hague convicts former President Thaci</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:389e324062d3eb6d03ecaea3ebee8d62a07c5a0e3680217e9e4c7c39bd05f18b</id><updated>2026-09-17T05:01:18Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T15:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/shock-in-kosovo-as-hague-convicts-former-president-thaci/a-79294916--a5436d550055.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/shock-in-kosovo-as-hague-convicts-former-president-thaci/a-79294916?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The conviction in The Hague of former President Hashim Thaci and three former Kosovo Liberation Army leaders has caused consternation in Kosovo — both among political leaders and on the streets. DW reports from Pristina.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>British-American writer Bonnie Greer dies aged 77</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:65198e48f9c045a8114abb8687c131ee18e9d2ecf8e522f270ce80249044fac0</id><updated>2026-09-17T05:01:18Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T15:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/british-american-writer-bonnie-greer-dies-aged-77/a-79293174--ca7cae1c3055.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/british-american-writer-bonnie-greer-dies-aged-77/a-79293174?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Chicago-born playwright Bonnie Greer, who became a familiar face in British political discourse later in life, has died. Her husband David Hutchins announced news of Greer's death.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Gaza: At least 21 dead, including children, in building collapse</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:506428107e06b8a94595405a85904f30a3ecb208ede42d1914c9427c7f08f654</id><updated>2026-09-17T05:01:18Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T15:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gaza-at-least-21-dead-including-children-in-building-collapse/a-79293453--3138d3baf4ea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gaza-at-least-21-dead-including-children-in-building-collapse/a-79293453?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The search for survivors has been hampered by Israeli restrictions on heavy machinery in the Gaza Strip. Authorities say 2,000 damaged buildings in the territory are occupied by families who have nowhere else to go.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Forgotten US court of 'secrecy' could mean more deportations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d5c8f223652580fe23344d707066f17ec32eb3894dee7bd51d90f4925e706637</id><updated>2026-09-17T05:01:18Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T15:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/forgotten-us-court-of-secrecy-could-mean-more-deportations/a-79291125--0ff5869fb815.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/forgotten-us-court-of-secrecy-could-mean-more-deportations/a-79291125?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The use of a secretive and long dormant court in the deportation of a woman from the US could have significant consequences. The Alien Terrorist Removal Court was just used for the first time in its 30-year history.</summary><category term="TOP STORIES" /></entry><entry><title>After Neuer: Who will be Germany's new No. 1 goalkeeper?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:97584c3aa6a175723b0dc3f1f5caa6d318ce6cecdde2f84b7031a5df7e1c3d52</id><updated>2026-09-17T05:01:18Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T14:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/after-neuer-who-will-be-germany-s-new-no-1-goalkeeper/a-79276377--1d35484fc587.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/after-neuer-who-will-be-germany-s-new-no-1-goalkeeper/a-79276377?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Following Manuel Neuer's retirement, there are many candidates to succeed him, but which goalkeeper will Jürgen Klopp choose? What factors will play a role? And will Neuer's future have an indirect influence?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>How the Houthis are also putting Egypt under pressure</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b4696ea38ab83ba9b3b03ec743b89367bf40b69aa1205f5ffbd02e5644d5674d</id><updated>2026-09-17T05:01:18Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T13:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-the-houthis-are-also-putting-egypt-under-pressure/a-79291103--b1d138b096dd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-the-houthis-are-also-putting-egypt-under-pressure/a-79291103?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Houthis, a Yemeni rebel group, are expanding their control of maritime corridors in the Red Sea area. Their target is their avowed enemy Saudi Arabia. But the military moves also endanger Egypt.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Iran: Activists sound alarm as regime seizes Baha'i assets</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cfb23b9f40640c92619edd9ccf3c20aa9c6f9a7a1ff4e57419ca0235dca484e0</id><updated>2026-09-17T05:01:18Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T13:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-activists-sound-alarm-as-regime-seizes-baha-i-assets/a-79291138--d67cdfeb619f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-activists-sound-alarm-as-regime-seizes-baha-i-assets/a-79291138?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Rights groups warn Iran is increasingly confiscating assets from government critics and members of the country's Baha'i faith, but also actors, athletes and journalists living abroad.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Poland reaffirms support for Ukraine after drone strikes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:71ee9d06e1ea2c3ee225a528450f1ebbdf7d01a3945b57661b8d0e2d6e71681d</id><updated>2026-09-17T05:01:18Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T12:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/poland-reaffirms-support-for-ukraine-after-drone-strikes/a-79291144--da0463d9d7dc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/poland-reaffirms-support-for-ukraine-after-drone-strikes/a-79291144?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After Russia's recent drone attacks on targets close to the Ukraine-Poland border, Warsaw has doubled down on its support for Kyiv and pledged a "nonprovocative but serious response" to Moscow.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Belarus to release 25 more prisoners as US eases sanctions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0852106e632b72885bccd719f5f15d93af1f108022bbed70ff49b6c3348fc743</id><updated>2026-09-17T05:01:18Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T12:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/belarus-to-release-25-more-prisoners-as-us-eases-sanctions/a-79290676--44b5cc402b01.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/belarus-to-release-25-more-prisoners-as-us-eases-sanctions/a-79290676?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Belarus will release 25 more prisoners under an interim agreement with the United States, while Washington plans to lift sanctions on two Belarusian companies and pursue broader negotiations.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Congo's Ebola epidemic may have gone undetected for months</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1812ba865db49b30499724790aabb9608c96260e0471df8f52af0e59e2b88df3</id><updated>2026-09-17T05:01:18Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T11:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/congo-s-ebola-epidemic-may-have-gone-undetected-for-months/a-79281803--d84e2884bf66.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/congo-s-ebola-epidemic-may-have-gone-undetected-for-months/a-79281803?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The deadliest Ebola outbreak on record in the Democratic Republic of Congo may have begun months before it was first declared in May.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India news: US bill sanctioning Russia could hit India with tariffs of up to 100%</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:50d9cd92717e75adb2ac4f32440b37d0cbbd2be043ca6a2075ed13b9d62cdfa1</id><updated>2026-09-17T05:01:18Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T11:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-us-bill-sanctioning-russia-could-hit-india-with-tariffs-of-up-to-100/live-79285577--613ee224f2db.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-us-bill-sanctioning-russia-could-hit-india-with-tariffs-of-up-to-100/live-79285577?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A new bill could give President Trump the power to impose tariffs of up to 100% on countries buying Russian oil and gas, potentially affecting major importer India.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
